          "note": "B. Stereoisomerism: a main subheading of 11.10.1 Types of isomerism, its own page (owner 2026-11-04); PDF 268-268."
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Stereoisomers are such compounds which possess the same structural formula, but differ with respect to the positions of the identical groups in space. It is part of class 12 syllabus and will be covered there."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "There are two types of stereoisomerism;"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": true,
            "items": [
              "Geometrical or cis trans isomerism",
              "Optical isomerism"
            ],
            "marker": "i."
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
